D3D12: an attachment resolve lands in the destination view's mip and resolves every layer.

EndRendering computes the destination subresource with the resource's array size where
GetSubresourceIndex takes its mip count, and resolves only the view's first layer, although its
barriers cover them all. NRI's main fixed both in 48d4a33 ("array layers and destination mip
indexing"); this backports those two lines' worth to v190 and leaves the rest of 48d4a33 (the new
resolve accesses and stages) to the tag that carries it. Drop it with that tag.

Measured on v190, NVIDIA, debug layer and NRI validation on: a resolve into the view of mip 1,
layer 1 of a two-mip, three-layer texture left that subresource as it was (it went to subresource
4); into layer 1 of a one-mip, two-layer texture it gave "[877] ... subresource index is out of
bounds" and Close failed; a two-layer view resolved only layer 0. Vulkan was right in all three.
With the change D3D12 resolves into the view's mip and layer, and every layer of it.

diff --git a/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp b/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
index 0bcb9af..3905244 100644
--- a/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
+++ b/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
@@ -1969,9 +1969,13 @@ NRI_INLINE void CommandBufferD3D12::EndRendering() {
             ID3D12Resource* dstResource = attachmentDesc->resolveDst->GetResource();
             D3D12_RESOURCE_DESC dstResourceDesc = dstResource->GetDesc();
             const TexViewDesc& dstDesc = attachmentDesc->resolveDst->GetTexViewDesc();
-            uint32_t dstSubresource = GetSubresourceIndex(dstDesc.layerOffset, dstResourceDesc.DepthOrArraySize, dstDesc.mipOffset, dstResourceDesc.DepthOrArraySize, planeBits);
+            uint32_t dstSubresource = GetSubresourceIndex(dstDesc.layerOffset, dstResourceDesc.DepthOrArraySize, dstDesc.mipOffset, dstResourceDesc.MipLevels, planeBits);
 
-            GetGraphicsCommandList()->ResolveSubresourceRegion(dstResource, dstSubresource, 0, 0, srcResource, srcSubresource, nullptr, format.typed, resolveMode);
+            for (uint32_t layer = 0; layer < srcDesc.layerNum; layer++) {
+                GetGraphicsCommandList()->ResolveSubresourceRegion(dstResource, dstSubresource, 0, 0, srcResource, srcSubresource, nullptr, format.typed, resolveMode);
+                srcSubresource += srcResourceDesc.MipLevels;
+                dstSubresource += dstResourceDesc.MipLevels;
+            }
         }
 
         // Restore state
